From a61af6662cbba8aa33d2075fb077147bf56134f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Edward Wiles <emmabenzvi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 20:44:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Implement CM-aware C+ gradient backend behind explicit
 cm_gradient_backend selector

New file lfix_cm_cplus.jl (purely additive): with_q0_C, build_lfix_base_cache_cm_C!,
composite_gradient_at_Cplus_from_cache, composite_gradient_at_Cplus_cm, and the cb_G! entry
point cm_production_gradient_cplus. Composes the existing factorized Backend C+ economic-block
builder (build_lfix_base_cache_C!, unmodified) with the existing CM fixed-contribution term
(cm_fixed_contribution, unmodified, shared with the Reference CM path) per the decomposition
derived in docs/CM_GRADIENT_ALGEBRA_TRACE_2026-07-22.md. No existing function is modified;
composite_gradient_at_Cplus (the live unrestricted-path production function) is untouched.

cm_checkpoint.jl: adds cm_gradient_backend::Symbol=:reference kwarg to
run_cm_upper_checkpointed, validated, logged explicitly at startup, and recorded to a
<label>_gradient_backend.txt sidecar next to the checkpoint (does not touch CMCheckpoint's
binary schema, so resume/schema compatibility is unaffected). cb_G! dispatches to
cm_production_gradient_cplus only when cm_gradient_backend=:cplus; the default :reference path
is byte-identical to before this commit. Pool/workspace for :cplus are built once per run and
are nothing (zero cost) when :reference is in effect.

cm_production_stage_runner.jl: adds lfix_cm_cplus.jl to the include chain (after
cm_production_bundle.jl, before cm_outer_driver.jl/cm_checkpoint.jl).

Both new/edited files parse cleanly (Meta.parseall). Not yet run against real KNITRO --
correctness battery is the next commit.
